# SRG-APP-000098-WSR-000060  -  CAT II
# A web server, behind a load balancer or proxy server, must produce log
# records containing the client IP information as the source and destination
# and not the load balancer or proxy IP information with each event.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000098-WSR-000060
group:           V-206363
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      documented
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000133
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    Where a reverse proxy or load balancer fronts the instance, Splunk can be
                 told so: tools.proxy.on makes its HTTP services use the X-Forwarded-*
                 headers for access request logging instead of the immediate client's
                 address.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] tools.proxy.base https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] tools.proxy.on https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Whether a proxy or load balancer fronts the instance decides whether this
                 requirement applies at all - the check text makes it not applicable
                 otherwise - and that is read from the network architecture documentation.
external:        The fronting proxy must insert the client address in an X-Forwarded-For
                 header; Splunk can only consume a header the device sends.
external:        Whether a reverse proxy or load balancer fronts this instance at all,
                 which decides whether the requirement has a configuration surface here;
                 where one is present, web.conf [settings] tools.proxy.on must be true and
                 tools.proxy.base must carry a scheme as well as a host and port.
external:        The proxy's own insertion of the X-Forwarded-For header, without which
                 tools.proxy.on has no client address to record.

manual_reason:   The requirement applies to a web server that sits behind a load balancer
                 or proxy server, and it asks that the access record carry the client
                 address rather than the proxy address. web.conf [settings] tools.proxy.on
                 and tools.proxy.base tell Splunk Web that a proxy is in front of it, so
                 they are correctly unset where none is, and asserting them unconditionally
                 reports a finding against an instance that is reached directly. Whether a
                 proxy fronts the instance is an architecture fact outside the
                 configuration, so the assessor establishes that first and then reads the
                 two settings.

citation:        SCOPE drift within the product, and OVER-REACH. Removed inputs.conf
                 [http://<name>] connection_host equals proxied_ip. That setting governs
                 how the HTTP Event Collector stamps host on ingested events -
                 inputs.conf.spec documents proxied_ip only in the [http://name] token
                 stanza, where it "checks whether an X-Forwarded-For header was sent... and
                 if so, sets the host to that value" - which is data ingestion, not the web
                 server's own access logging that this requirement covers. An instance with
                 no HEC token input, or whose HEC is not fronted by the proxy, would be
                 failed for a control it satisfies. The determined row also carries no
                 stanza, so the placeholder could not have matched.
finding:         The instance is fronted by a proxy or load balancer but tools.proxy.on is
                 not enabled with a tools.proxy.base, so its access records carry the
                 proxy's address rather than the client's.
